{"name":"Peace & Quiet","hex":"#e0dac8","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"peace","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A state of tranquility, quiet, and harmony. For instance, a state free from civil disturbance.","A feeling of tranquility, free from oppressive and unpleasant thoughts and emotions."]},{"part":"Interjection","definitions":["Shut up!, silence!; be quiet, be silent.","Peace out; goodbye."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/peace"},{"term":"quiet","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["With little or no sound; free of disturbing noise.","Having little motion or activity; calm."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To cause (someone or something) to become quiet.","To become quiet or calm."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/quiet"}],"entries":[{"title":"Peace & Quiet","blocks":[{"text":"\"Peace & Quiet\" was the first official release from the British indie rock band The Rifles. It was released only on 7\" by Blow Up Records and was limited to only 1000 copies. Upon hearing a demo of \"Peace & Quiet\" in late 2004, BBC Radio 1 host Zane Lowe immediately invited The Rifles to the Radio 1 studios to record a session, which aired in December of that year."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/0/07/Peace%26QuietBUR.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Peace_%26_Quiet"},{"title":"Peace","blocks":[{"text":"Peace is a state of harmony in the absence of hostility and violence. In a societal sense, peace is commonly used to mean a lack of conflict and freedom from fear of violence between individuals or groups."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d0/Peace_dove_%283329620077%29.jpg/330px-Peace_dove_%283329620077%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Peace"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://upload.w